  "question": {
    "text": "Consider two G.Ps. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><msup><mn>4</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mn>4</mn><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo></math>&nbsp;of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>60</mn></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math> terms respectively. If the geometric mean of all the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>60</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi></math>&nbsp;terms is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced><mfrac><mn>225</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac></msup></math>, then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><munderover><mo>&#8721;</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mi>k</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is equal to:",
